hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18473","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Salamah ibn Nuaym, and he was of the companions of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah associating nothing with Him enters Paradise, even if he commits adultery and even if he steals."
"22831","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Salamah ibn Nuaym, and he was of the companions of the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever meets Allah not associating anything with Him will enter Paradise, even if he commits adultery and even if he steals."
